Package: kolibri
Type: Package
Title: Kernel-Operations for Long-read Insertion, Breakpoint and Recombination Inspection
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Grey", "Monroe",
      email = "greymonroe@gmail.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
    )
  )
Description: Tools for inspecting long-read alignments (PacBio/ONT) exported as BED12
    to find, group, and visualize split reads. Split reads—reads that map to two or
    more genomic locations—are indicators of structural variation, transposable element
    insertions, recombination breakpoints, and assembly errors. kolibri clusters
    these split segments per chromosome using sweep, DBSCAN, or kernel-density-based
    algorithms, builds a shared-read network connecting related clusters, and provides
    a suite of visualization functions for exploring the network and individual nodes.
